{
 ;; the agent's record as one map, @ctx (seon.ctx): its environment, its own attributes and its
 ;; pattern's joins by their keys; the page draws it as a block (seon.render.ui/ctx), the model reads it
 ;; through the one printer (no :ai render)
 :seon.ctx/ctx [:map {:seon.render/hiccup seon.render.ui/ctx} [:t :int] [:branch :seon.db/branch] [:commit {:optional true} :uuid]]
 ;; a swap! of @ctx refused, nothing written (seon.ctx/write!): a value its schema refuses, or a key
 ;; with no schema, each with where it is and why
 ;; the state a proof is shown in (seon.ctx.status/status derives it; the stored verdict is :seon.test/status): each member's
 ;; title and its explanation, Markdown, what it means and what the agent does next, which the status render draws for the person
 ;; and the model alike (docs/render.md#how-the-work-stands)
 :seon.ctx.status/proof-state
 [:enum {:seon.status/title {:pass "green" :fail "red" :error "red" :undefined "not written" :not-run "no verdict" :deferred "runs at merge" :unknown "not judged yet"}
         :seon.status/explain
         {:pass "Passed on your code as it is now. Nothing to do for it."
          :fail "An assertion failed: each one and what it got is shown. Change the code, or the test if the test is wrong, then `(prove)`."
          :error "The test threw before it could judge: the error is shown. Fix what threw, then `(prove)`."
          :undefined "Your branch has no test by this name. Write it where the page says, then `(prove)`."
          :not-run "The test run itself failed, so nothing was judged. Fix what stopped the run (shown above it); proving again before that fails the same way."
          :deferred "It starts a process of its own, so it runs when your task merges, not in your turn. Nothing to do for it now."
          :unknown "No verdict yet for your code as it is now. `(prove)` runs it."}
         :description "The state a proof is shown in, judged from its stored verdict and the task (seon.ctx.status/status). See docs/render.md#how-the-work-stands."}
  :pass :fail :error :undefined :not-run :deferred :unknown]
 :seon.ctx/invalid [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.ctx/invalid]]
                                           [:invalid [:vector [:map [:path [:vector :any]] [:why :any]]]]]]
 ;; written, the db would not hold what the swap! says at these paths (it would hold :held)
 :seon.ctx/not-held [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.ctx/not-held]]
                                            [:paths [:vector [:vector :any]]] [:held [:vector :any]]]]
 ;; the swap!'s map is not of the record's basis: its :t, :branch or :commit differs (the db moved while
 ;; the swap!'s function ran, or the function wrote one of them, which are the environment's), it is
 ;; no map (a reset! of the atom), or there is no record yet (:held empty)
 :seon.ctx/basis [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.ctx/basis]]
                                         [:held :map] [:swapped :map]]]
 ;; a pattern the walk cannot read (seon.ctx/spec): no vector, an option neither pull's nor :by, a
 ;; join naming no attribute or with no pattern; the clause it stopped at
 :seon.ctx/invalid-pattern [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.ctx/invalid-pattern]] [:clause :any]]]
 ;; metadata on the value of a join a :limit windows (seon.ctx/join writes it; seon.print.emit reads it to say how many more there are)
 :seon.ctx/count [:int {:min 0 :description "How many members a windowed join has in the db, as metadata on the value the context holds for it, which holds only the window: (:seon.ctx/count (meta (:seon.eval/_agent @ctx))). Absent when no :limit made the value. See docs/ctx.md#the-pattern."}]
 ;; a join's option in a pull pattern, [:attribute :seon.ctx/below pattern] (seon.render/again reads it)
 :seon.ctx/below [:sequential {:description "A join's option in a pull pattern: what a join asked to a depth asks below its last level, in place of asking itself again. Read by seon.render/again. See docs/ctx.md#the-pattern."} :any]
 ;; a record whose identity attributes name entity schemas none of which extends the others (seon.render/entity-schema):
 ;; no one schema names it, so no pattern, render or layout does; the schemas it named
 :seon.render/no-one-schema [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.render/no-one-schema]] [:schemas [:vector :qualified-keyword]]]]
 ;; an entity no render renders (seon.render/render-var-of): its schema, nil when none names it, names no :seon.render/hiccup and extends none that does
 ;; its schema and its identity attributes
 :seon.render/no-render [:and :seon.error/base [:map [:seon.error/type [:= :seon.render/no-render]] [:schema [:maybe :qualified-keyword]] [:identity [:vector :qualified-keyword]]]]
 ;; a pattern as the walk takes it (seon.render/pattern): '* or the attributes it names, those asked with their transaction (:txs: the key each fills), the keys the db fills at this path (:ro), and its joins,
 ;; each with its own pattern under :sub
 :seon.ctx/spec [:map [:star? :boolean] [:attrs [:set :keyword]] [:txs {:optional true} [:map-of :keyword :keyword]] [:ro {:optional true} [:set :keyword]]
                 [:joins [:vector [:map [:attr :qualified-keyword] [:key :keyword] [:rev? :boolean] [:by [:maybe :qualified-keyword]]
                                   [:reverse? :boolean] [:limit [:maybe nat-int?]] [:tx {:optional true} :keyword] [:sub :map]]]]]
 ;; the walk's state beside a record's map (seon.ctx/node): every path each entity sits at (:at {e #{path}}, an entity
 ;; built whole at each, as d/pull holds it), each path's pattern (:spec {path spec}: two paths can pull one entity by
 ;; different sub-patterns), what each join [e key] watches ([attribute value] keys, :watch) and its reverse (:watching);
 ;; each a map checked shallowly: a contract checked on every call of the walk must not cost what the walk is proven not to (the record's size)
 :seon.ctx/ix [:map [:at {:optional true} :map] [:spec {:optional true} :map]
               [:watch {:optional true} :map] [:watching {:optional true} :map]
               ;; the entity index (seon.db/index-of) the record's pattern and joins read schemas in; built again by a patch that moved a schema entry
               [:index {:optional true} :map] [:own-index? {:optional true} :boolean]]}
